The icon set in `src/icon/` (shipped compiled into `dist/`) is substantially
derived from Feather and Lucide. Provenance was established on 2026-08-05 by
comparing all 88 shipped icons against feather-icons 4.29.2, lucide-static
1.28.0, heroicons 2.2.0, bootstrap-icons 1.13.1 and @tabler/icons 3.46.0 —
11,564 icons in all — matching on normalised path data rather than on file
name, since many icons are shipped here under a different name (for example
`close` = Feather `x`, `email` = `mail`, `spinner` = `loader`, `refresh` =
`refresh-cw`, `trash` = `trash-2`, `mute` = `volume-x`, `volume` = `volume-2`,
`info-circle` = `info`, `thumb-up` = `thumbs-up`, `loading` = Lucide
`loader-circle`).

  - 68 icons are identical to a Feather icon.
  - 12 icons are identical to a Lucide icon (`eraser`, `grip-vertical`,
    `hourglass`, `list-ordered`, `loading`, `maximize`, `minimize`, `project`,
    `repeat`, `square`, `strikethrough`, `unlink`).
  - 8 icons (`chart`, `grid`, `pdf`, `pip`, `send`, `settings`, `skip-back`,
    `skip-forward`) match nothing in Feather, Lucide, Heroicons, Bootstrap
    Icons or Tabler — 11,564 icons compared. That is not proof they are
    original, only that they do not come from the sets that were checked.

This breakdown is checked on every audit run — see `scripts/icon-provenance.json`
and `npm run check:icons:provenance`. If an icon is added or changed so that its
provenance no longer matches that file, the build fails and this notice has to be
brought back in line.

